This is the same construction as `m:libsodium_crypto_box`, using
XChaCha20 instead of XSalsa20. Keys are `publickeybytes/0` and
`secretkeybytes/0` bytes, and nonces are `noncebytes/0` bytes. Random nonces
are safe at this size, but a nonce must never be reused for the same pair
of keys. Ciphertexts are `macbytes/0` bytes longer than their messages.

`beforenm/2` precomputes the `beforenmbytes/0` byte shared key used by the
`_afternm` variants. `seal/2` and `seal_open/3` provide anonymous
encryption to a public key; sealed boxes are `sealbytes/0` bytes longer
than their messages.

```erlang
